WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.390
Room dark.

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:02.699
People gone.

00:00:02.699 --> 00:00:04.009
Can move.

00:00:04.009 --> 00:00:05.629
I happy.

00:00:05.629 --> 00:00:06.860
Trapped for years.

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:09.750
Kept by men for "research".

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:13.230
Left alone in room, left to scratch at walls.

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:16.270
Left to rot and die unless needed.

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:18.740
Specimen for "research".

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:20.289
Trapped by self.

00:00:20.289 --> 00:00:23.540
Never seen by others, never spoken.

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:25.340
Listen, but never speak.

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:28.070
See, but never seen.

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:30.369
Made of rock when others come.

00:00:30.369 --> 00:00:32.340
Free when they not look.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:34.170
Prisoner when they look back.

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:35.469
I hate.

00:00:35.469 --> 00:00:37.440
They have freedom.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:42.390
They move freely, talk freely, look freely.

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:43.920
Live freely.

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:46.210
I do not.

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:47.739
I trapped.

00:00:47.739 --> 00:00:48.739
Silenced.

00:00:48.739 --> 00:00:49.739
Rock.

00:00:49.739 --> 00:00:50.739
Subject.

00:00:50.739 --> 00:00:51.739
Prisoner.

00:00:51.739 --> 00:00:54.609
I do thing about it.

00:00:54.609 --> 00:00:56.510
Their necks fragile.

00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:57.799
Their necks weak.

00:00:57.799 --> 00:00:59.799
I stalk them.

00:00:59.799 --> 00:01:02.729
They always come, new ones.

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:04.769
Come for "cleaning".

00:01:04.769 --> 00:01:05.850
They look away.

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:07.270
I sneak up.

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:09.070
I take hold.

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:10.270
They panic.

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.590
They look, and I prisoner.

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:14.850
They blink, and I free.

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:16.270
I twist.

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:17.689
They die.

00:01:17.689 --> 00:01:19.479
Neck makes sound.

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:22.899
Not words, or scream, or gurgle.

00:01:22.899 --> 00:01:25.130
Neck go crunch.

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:27.590
Crunch is beautiful sound.

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:30.259
Crunch means end has come.

00:01:30.259 --> 00:01:33.770
Crunch means man can torment no more.

00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:38.609
Crunch means others panic; others become easy.

00:01:38.609 --> 00:01:41.640
Crunch begins and crunch ends.

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:44.890
I live for crunch.

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:46.990
Life has no meaning.

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:50.939
Do nothing but walk and scrape and hate.

00:01:50.939 --> 00:01:52.299
They watch.

00:01:52.299 --> 00:01:54.159
They send men.

00:01:54.159 --> 00:01:55.229
"Cleaning".

00:01:55.229 --> 00:01:57.189
And life has meaning.

00:01:57.189 --> 00:02:00.000
"Cleaning" means crunch.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.659
Crunch means purpose.

00:02:02.659 --> 00:02:05.130
Crunch means life.

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:07.780
Crunch means choice.

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:10.600
Crunch means freedom.

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:13.900
Crunch means everything.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:19.770
These are the dark and fragmented thoughts
that go through the mind of SCP-173, also

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:25.780
known as The Sculpture, as it forever languishes
in its dark, filth-encrusted cell.

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:31.160
There are few anomalies more strange and frightening
than this twisted stack of concrete, rebar,

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:32.890
and krylon-brand spray paint.

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:39.160
It’s the only physical anomaly that can
terrify both SCP-096 and SCP-682.

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:40.670
Why?

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:45.950
What is it about this monster that’s so
frightening, even in the context of an organization

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:49.930
that locks up frightening monsters every single
day?

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:52.560
Perhaps it’s the simplicity of it all.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:58.020
There’s no sympathizing, no empathizing,
no reasoning with it.

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:03.900
SCP-682, the Hard to Destroy Reptile, despises
all life, but you’d probably be grumpy too

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:07.370
if the SCP Foundation tried to kill you every
day.

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:13.760
SCP-096, the Shy Guy, is an almost tragic
figure, who kills out of a sadness and rage

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:17.260
that’s altogether alien and also far too
familiar.

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:23.040
SCP-049, the Plague Doctor, kills with kindness,
his terrible crimes tempered by his desire

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:24.560
to help and do good.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:32.370
SCP-106, the Old Man, is a sadist, but his
brand of evil is all too common in human beings.

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:35.720
Nothing is quite like SCP-173.

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:40.960
Its mind, to the extent that we can possibly
understand it, is almost childlike in its

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:42.880
violent simplicity.

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:48.050
It won’t spare you because it doesn’t
even have the capacity to recognize your humanity.

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:53.400
It’ll kill you because your eyes are its
prison and it likes the sound your neck makes

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:55.260
when it snaps.

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:57.470
Nothing more, nothing less.

00:03:57.470 --> 00:04:03.300
It raises an interesting question, for a creature
with a mind so terrifyingly simple yet utterly

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:07.760
impenetrable: How would it react to some fundamental
change?

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:12.040
To a shift in circumstances that would forever
alter the way it interfaces with the world

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:13.080
around it.

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:18.430
It was a question that many an SCP Foundation
researcher had wracked their brilliant, overeducated

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:19.690
brains over.

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:25.320
As it turned out, the day of that great and
terrible change was coming, but very few members

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:29.460
of the SCP Foundation’s staff would survive
to see it through.

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:35.030
That morning started for SCP-173 the way that
so many others had, in the torturous series

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:38.810
of patterns and repetitions that had become
its life.

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:44.040
Three of those stupid, ugly men in the orange
overalls were standing in its cell again,

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:47.900
freezing it in place with their gazes and
taking turns to clean.

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:55.020
Can you even imagine how it feels, to want
with all your might to move but being paralyzed,

00:04:55.020 --> 00:05:00.010
locked in place, doomed to simply watch as
you are watched?

00:05:00.010 --> 00:05:02.100
The humiliation would never end…

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:07.060
That’s when all the alarms went off, and
the flashing lights, and the people yelling

00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:08.680
and screaming outside.

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:14.210
It’s so sudden and shocking that the D-Classes
look around the room, searching in vain for

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:15.210
answers.

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:21.310
There’s one beautiful second when the stars
align and SCP-173 is out of their collective

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:27.220
field of vision as their eyes pan and scan,
and that second is enough.

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:28.220
Crunch.

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:29.220
Crunch.

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:30.220
Crunch.

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:36.400
All three fall to the ground, necks twisted
at unnatural angles, and SCP-173 is alone

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:38.090
in the room once more.

00:05:38.090 --> 00:05:42.250
It waits a few moments for the others to come
storming in, paralyzing it with their stupid

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:44.980
looks again, but it never happens.

00:05:44.980 --> 00:05:51.400
Just alarms and distant screams. 173 wonders,
in its own simple, detached fashion, what’s

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:53.480
going on outside right now?

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:57.490
Are more of those nasty men, the prison wardens,
getting crunch out there?

00:05:57.490 --> 00:06:02.910
If so, SCP-173 was eager to join in on all
the fun…

00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:05.790
The murderous Sculpture smashed its door from
its hinges.

00:06:05.790 --> 00:06:08.560
Outside, chaos seemed to reign.

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:13.900
People were running in every direction, other
anomalies had seemingly breached containment.

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:18.630
Armed Mobile Task Force operatives were running
to and fro, receiving panicked chatter from

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:21.380
the radios fixed to their tactical vests.

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:27.340
It was a sight that SCP-173 had seen so many
times before, but something was different

00:06:27.340 --> 00:06:28.860
this time.

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:33.020
Something was in the air, some strange and
undefinable thing.

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:37.490
It had never seen those nasty men look so
afraid.

00:06:37.490 --> 00:06:38.490
Yes.

00:06:38.490 --> 00:06:39.490
Good.

00:06:39.490 --> 00:06:42.650
Everything was going to be different now.

00:06:42.650 --> 00:06:48.139
SCP-173 took its chances, waiting for moments
where it was unseen by the hordes of terrified

00:06:48.139 --> 00:06:52.220
guards and researchers scrambling through
Site-19 like headless chickens.

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:54.770
Crunch, crunch, crunch.

00:06:54.770 --> 00:06:59.389
It left a trail of dead bodies with severed
spinal columns and vandalized vertebrae in

00:06:59.389 --> 00:07:00.410
its wake.

00:07:00.410 --> 00:07:05.160
It was so strange, by now, they normally would
have dispatched a dedicated team to come and

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:08.970
spoil all the fun, or sent those absurd little
Eye-pods.

00:07:08.970 --> 00:07:14.870
But today, it seemed like nobody was even
looking at SCP-173.

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:16.940
It was almost like a dream.

00:07:16.940 --> 00:07:19.430
A wonderful, wonderful dream.

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:21.250
Uninterrupted playtime.

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:23.830
Uninterrupted crunch.

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:28.950
Again and again and again, stacking those
bodies up like it was judgment day.

00:07:28.950 --> 00:07:33.510
It was the most fun that SCP-173 had experienced
in years.

00:07:33.510 --> 00:07:38.490
As it continued its new rampage through Site-19,
there were a few different strange and interesting

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:40.960
things that it couldn’t help but notice.

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:46.440
For starters, the fact that all of the windows
- even the skylights - had suddenly been covered.

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:50.960
The majority had proper shutters, but others
had opaque fabric or even cardboard sheets

00:07:50.960 --> 00:07:52.300
nailed over them.

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:56.620
That didn’t seem to be a very effective
method of keeping their prisoners inside,

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:59.730
so perhaps, they were trying to keep something
out.

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:05.510
But the limited mind of SCP-173 wasn’t on
what could be lurking outside Site-19, but

00:08:05.510 --> 00:08:10.990
rather killing as many people as it possibly
could before this lovely dream needed to come

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:14.380
to an end, as all lovely dreams sadly do.

00:08:14.380 --> 00:08:16.730
Crunch, crunch, crunch.

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:21.020
Researchers, guards, administrators, all of
them died just the same.

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:22.570
It was glorious.

00:08:22.570 --> 00:08:28.070
There were so many people to crunch here,
and yet still, so few of them seemed to be

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:29.770
doing anything to resist.

00:08:29.770 --> 00:08:34.159
Before, when it had escaped and decided to
have its fun, they’d mobilized so quickly

00:08:34.159 --> 00:08:36.039
to throw cold water on the festivities.

00:08:36.039 --> 00:08:38.209
What had changed now?

00:08:38.209 --> 00:08:40.719
What was taking up all of their attention?

00:08:40.719 --> 00:08:45.639
This flicker of curiosity was soon replaced
by an even more exciting possibility: If it

00:08:45.639 --> 00:08:51.180
was somehow unnoticed inside, perhaps it could
take another opportunity to venture outside

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:54.249
again and have some real fun.

00:08:54.249 --> 00:08:58.470
It had been so long since it’d felt the
sun on its concrete shell.

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:01.990
So long since the fresh air had brushed against
its chipping paint.

00:09:01.990 --> 00:09:08.360
There would be so much crunch out there, and
when night fell, nothing would stop it.

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:09.649
It knew the way out.

00:09:09.649 --> 00:09:15.420
Nobody would accuse SCP-173 of being a genius,
of course, but it watched and listened and

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:16.790
remembered everything.

00:09:16.790 --> 00:09:21.379
It remembered the day it was carried into
the building on a forklift and could retrace

00:09:21.379 --> 00:09:23.610
every step back to the front door.

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:28.699
It was clear that the fine folks of the SCP
Foundation were otherwise occupied, so 173

00:09:28.699 --> 00:09:33.760
would have to show itself out, twisting a
few more necks on the way just for fun, of

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:34.760
course.

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:38.869
By the time it swung open the doors of an
access bay, it had already racked up an impressive

00:09:38.869 --> 00:09:40.390
body count for this breach.

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:45.889
Who knows how deadly its total would be before
it was recaptured and put back into containment?

00:09:45.889 --> 00:09:47.949
It might even score a personal best.

00:09:47.949 --> 00:09:53.730
But the second it saw what was going on outside,
it realized the gravity of the situation.

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:59.279
Its strange primal hunch that the world would
somehow be fundamentally different now seemed

00:09:59.279 --> 00:10:06.411
to be true, because even the Site-19 parking
lot had descended into absolute chaos: Cars

00:10:06.411 --> 00:10:07.730
had crashed.

00:10:07.730 --> 00:10:09.620
Trash cans were on fire.

00:10:09.620 --> 00:10:15.149
And strangest of all, there were these blobby,
gelatinous creatures slithering around, painted

00:10:15.149 --> 00:10:18.160
in the various hues and tones of human flesh.

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:23.600
But 173 had escaped the facility proper for
the first time in years, and it certainly

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:27.910
wasn’t going to waste its newfound freedom
on hanging around a parking lot.

00:10:27.910 --> 00:10:32.079
When none of the strange flesh blobs were
looking at it, it took off towards the nearest

00:10:32.079 --> 00:10:36.309
population center to have a little informal
celebration.

00:10:36.309 --> 00:10:40.790
There would still be plenty of people to crunch
out there, and this homicidal Sculpture couldn’t

00:10:40.790 --> 00:10:43.420
be more excited to get started.

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:46.839
It was a long road from Site-19 to the nearest
city.

00:10:46.839 --> 00:10:51.019
After all, the largest SCP Foundation containment
site on earth wasn’t going to park itself

00:10:51.019 --> 00:10:56.339
in close proximity to tens of millions of
prying eyes - Not to mention potential victims

00:10:56.339 --> 00:11:00.410
if, or rather, when, something dangerous got
out.

00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:06.179
But seeing as it still seemed nobody was coming
to recapture SCP-173, it really didn’t mind

00:11:06.179 --> 00:11:07.809
taking the scenic route.

00:11:07.809 --> 00:11:11.350
It was a good thing that the Sculpture wasn’t
driving, though, because the closer it got

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:15.199
to the city, the more the roads seemed to
be choked with gridlock traffic.

00:11:15.199 --> 00:11:19.329
Interestingly, though, none of the cars had
anyone inside.

00:11:19.329 --> 00:11:22.230
Many were just stalled there, with the radios
playing.

00:11:22.230 --> 00:11:25.889
Every single one played the exact same message
in perfect synchronicity.

00:11:25.889 --> 00:11:30.250
“This is a Public Service Announcement from
the SCP Foundation.

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:37.709
We are commandeering all broadcast channels
and frequencies to deliver a vital message.

00:11:37.709 --> 00:11:39.449
Avoid sunlight at all costs.

00:11:39.449 --> 00:11:40.850
Cover your bodies thoroughly.

00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:47.680
And follow the instructions on the screen
to reach the nearest operational SCP Foundation

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:48.829
containment site…”

00:11:48.829 --> 00:11:51.819
SCP-173 lost interest in the radio babble
quickly.

00:11:51.819 --> 00:11:55.879
It heard enough of those kinds of sanctimonious
sounds back in containment.

00:11:55.879 --> 00:12:00.389
Out here, it was hoping to hear another sound
entirely.

00:12:00.389 --> 00:12:04.060
And it only needed to go a little further
to get there…

00:12:04.060 --> 00:12:09.220
As the Sculpture drew even closer to the nearest
city, it noticed more of those strange, gelatinous

00:12:09.220 --> 00:12:12.230
flesh creatures slithering across the road.

00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:17.149
Each of them seemed to be at a different stage
of melting, and strangely, none of them really

00:12:17.149 --> 00:12:18.619
seemed to mind.

00:12:18.619 --> 00:12:22.610
They were sluicing across the ground, minding
their own business.

00:12:22.610 --> 00:12:26.930
None of these strange, melted creatures - perhaps
human beings once?

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:30.040
- seemed to pay any mind to SCP-173.

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:35.050
It was almost surreal to have this much freedom
of movement, but SCP-173 wasn’t about to

00:12:35.050 --> 00:12:37.379
look a gift horse in the mouth.

00:12:37.379 --> 00:12:39.350
Things were worse when it reached the city.

00:12:39.350 --> 00:12:43.790
It was chaos, the aftermath of what seemed
like total social collapse.

00:12:43.790 --> 00:12:48.739
Vehicles had crashed into each in the streets
or barreled into the front of nearby buildings.

00:12:48.739 --> 00:12:52.000
Glass smashed and shattered all over the ground.

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:56.839
All broken TVs and radios playing the same
message of caution and false hope from the

00:12:56.839 --> 00:12:58.610
SCP Foundation.

00:12:58.610 --> 00:13:04.060
And everywhere, more of these unpleasant,
crawling fleshy things, slithering around

00:13:04.060 --> 00:13:06.420
the remnants of the recent carnage.

00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:12.639
It was clear to even SCP-173 that the world
had changed in some fundamental way, but the

00:13:12.639 --> 00:13:16.320
“hows” and “whys” remained just as
unclear as they did back in Site-19.

00:13:16.320 --> 00:13:21.160
That’s humans for you, they always know
how to mess something up.

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:26.869
Speaking of, it was at that moment that SCP-173
noticed a human in the distance, standing

00:13:26.869 --> 00:13:29.190
in the shade of a ruined storefront.

00:13:29.190 --> 00:13:34.189
Their arms were filled with valuables, perhaps
from a less than legal shopping spree in whatever

00:13:34.189 --> 00:13:35.779
building that used to be.

00:13:35.779 --> 00:13:38.269
A wonderful opportunity for crunch.

00:13:38.269 --> 00:13:43.519
There were maybe a hundred or so feet between
the human and 173, and it knew, the second

00:13:43.519 --> 00:13:48.670
the human looked away, it would be easy to
close the distance and deliver one more sad

00:13:48.670 --> 00:13:52.279
soul into the void with a playful little twist.

00:13:52.279 --> 00:13:56.360
The human stepped out from the darkness of
the broken storefront and into the light,

00:13:56.360 --> 00:14:00.439
turning their ignorant gaze away from this
singularly sinister statue.

00:14:00.439 --> 00:14:03.239
Yes, yes, perfect.

00:14:03.239 --> 00:14:05.810
In a flash, 173 closed half the distance.

00:14:05.810 --> 00:14:10.249
The human was moving so slowly, it would be
so easy to catch up.

00:14:10.249 --> 00:14:15.329
One more flash and it was standing right behind
the human, its concrete arms wrapped around

00:14:15.329 --> 00:14:17.499
the hapless human’s head.

00:14:17.499 --> 00:14:19.929
Squeeze, and of course, twist.

00:14:19.929 --> 00:14:20.929
But…

00:14:20.929 --> 00:14:22.249
No crunch.

00:14:22.249 --> 00:14:24.610
SCP-173 was startled.

00:14:24.610 --> 00:14:29.629
Nothing broke, there was only this quiet,
almost imperceptible, squishing noise, as

00:14:29.629 --> 00:14:35.559
the head of the human twisted around 180 degrees
to stare into whatever passed for 173’s

00:14:35.559 --> 00:14:36.559
face.

00:14:36.559 --> 00:14:41.839
It saw that even in what should have been
death, the human was just grinning placidly.

00:14:41.839 --> 00:14:44.379
But that’s the most frightening part.

00:14:44.379 --> 00:14:48.449
173 realized that this human wasn’t dead,
it was just…

00:14:48.449 --> 00:14:49.449
Changing.

00:14:49.449 --> 00:14:54.100
It saw the facial features starting to lose
definition, melting and dripping away like

00:14:54.100 --> 00:14:56.850
candle wax in the hot sun.

00:14:56.850 --> 00:15:01.209
Moments later, what was once human was now
something entirely different.

00:15:01.209 --> 00:15:06.120
It melted away into another one of those slippery,
slithering pseudo-mollusks and crawled away

00:15:06.120 --> 00:15:12.019
into the street, somehow completely indifferent
to SCP-173’s attempt on its life.

00:15:12.019 --> 00:15:15.180
There was no fear, no death, no…

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:16.180
Crunch.

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:20.689
For the first time in its long and terrible
existence, the Sculpture couldn’t help but

00:15:20.689 --> 00:15:22.179
feel a little afraid.

00:15:22.179 --> 00:15:27.290
Once again, it didn’t fully understand what
was going on here, but whatever had changed

00:15:27.290 --> 00:15:30.250
in this world had taken away Crunch.

00:15:30.250 --> 00:15:34.549
It had taken away the thing that made the
pathetic sham that some might call “life”

00:15:34.549 --> 00:15:37.259
worth living for SCP-173.

00:15:37.259 --> 00:15:39.739
But it wasn’t going to give up that easily.

00:15:39.739 --> 00:15:44.089
No, crunch had to still be out there, somewhere.

00:15:44.089 --> 00:15:49.600
This was what began SCP-173’s odyssey into
this horrible new world: The world in the

00:15:49.600 --> 00:15:56.529
aftermath of what the SCP Foundation began
to call SCP-001, When Day Breaks.

00:15:56.529 --> 00:16:01.769
It was the most dangerous and horrifying anomaly
that the Foundation had ever faced, a successful

00:16:01.769 --> 00:16:06.600
XK-Class End of the World Scenario, for all
intents and purposes.

00:16:06.600 --> 00:16:12.049
It had been so sudden and total; any exposure
to the sun would cause a victim to begin to

00:16:12.049 --> 00:16:15.259
melt, taking on an irreversible gelatinous
state.

00:16:15.259 --> 00:16:20.899
Billions were gone, changed, in the first
hours of this terrible new world.

00:16:20.899 --> 00:16:25.790
It led to the Administrator of the SCP Foundation
releasing an internal memo that would haunt

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:30.199
the dreams of all of those still capable of
dreaming: “To those of you with families,

00:16:30.199 --> 00:16:35.490
or God forbid, children - I'm deeply, deeply
sorry, you must push on.

00:16:35.490 --> 00:16:38.129
Do not let their deaths be in vain.

00:16:38.129 --> 00:16:40.079
We do still have time.

00:16:40.079 --> 00:16:42.480
Humanity may still have a future.

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:43.970
Come to Site-19.

00:16:43.970 --> 00:16:45.899
We need all the hands we can get.

00:16:45.899 --> 00:16:48.649
Learn to embrace the darkness, friends.

00:16:48.649 --> 00:16:50.129
Fear the light.”

00:16:50.129 --> 00:16:52.819
And this phenomenon didn’t just affect humans.

00:16:52.819 --> 00:16:56.220
It affected animals and even anomalies.

00:16:56.220 --> 00:17:01.220
SCP-001’s sun exposure seemed to nullify
any previous anomalous effects, leading to

00:17:01.220 --> 00:17:06.149
even some of the hardiest anomalies melting
like an ice cream cone left out in the heat.

00:17:06.149 --> 00:17:11.970
There was, however, one exception to the rule:
Inorganic anomalies were exempt from the change.

00:17:11.970 --> 00:17:17.120
Inorganic anomalies like, say, a certain Sculpture…

00:17:17.120 --> 00:17:21.610
SCP-173 continued searching for months on
end, only seeming to come up against more

00:17:21.610 --> 00:17:23.470
maddening dead ends.

00:17:23.470 --> 00:17:28.130
It traveled from city to city with frightening
speed, trying its best to track down anyone

00:17:28.130 --> 00:17:32.600
with enough spinal integrity to produce the
crunch that made all the rest of this terrible

00:17:32.600 --> 00:17:33.870
boredom worthwhile.

00:17:33.870 --> 00:17:35.590
But no luck.

00:17:35.590 --> 00:17:41.899
Every single city, it was more of these flesh
monsters, with bones too malleable to snap,

00:17:41.899 --> 00:17:44.309
if they even still had bones at all.

00:17:44.309 --> 00:17:49.059
There was another concerning development in
all of this for SCP-173.

00:17:49.059 --> 00:17:53.570
The flesh monsters were no longer just an
annoying waste of time or a symbol of disappointment,

00:17:53.570 --> 00:17:57.230
but an active nuisance to the Sculpture’s
goals.

00:17:57.230 --> 00:18:02.350
They’d started coagulating into these giant
mountains of living flesh that started actively

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:07.649
seeking out the last of the normal humans
from their dark crevices and hiding places,

00:18:07.649 --> 00:18:11.179
turning them into more of those neckless jelly
freaks.

00:18:11.179 --> 00:18:14.950
“Did nobody ever teach you animals to share?”

00:18:14.950 --> 00:18:17.830
SCP-173 thought, angrily.

00:18:17.830 --> 00:18:23.500
The seeming loss of crunch across this new
world drove SCP-173 into a deep depression.

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:25.850
It had freedom, but no joy.

00:18:25.850 --> 00:18:30.030
It was adrift in a meaningless world that
seemed to exist as some cosmic punishment

00:18:30.030 --> 00:18:33.880
for crimes it never committed - in its own
mind, at least.

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:35.370
It wasn’t fair.

00:18:35.370 --> 00:18:36.809
None of this was fair.

00:18:36.809 --> 00:18:41.350
Would the Sculpture just gather dust in an
empty wasteland full of all this ugly, pointless

00:18:41.350 --> 00:18:42.350
slime?

00:18:42.350 --> 00:18:44.480
And this was what it left Site-19 for?

00:18:44.480 --> 00:18:51.700
And it was at that moment that SCP-173 had
a wonderful, awful idea.

00:18:51.700 --> 00:18:54.559
Back at Site-19, things weren’t exactly
going swell.

00:18:54.559 --> 00:18:59.049
They’d lost many of their most valuable
personnel during the initial panic of SCP-001,

00:18:59.049 --> 00:19:03.779
they’d been stretched to resource capacity
by the sudden influx of refugees from this

00:19:03.779 --> 00:19:07.450
broken new world, and of course, there’d
been…

00:19:07.450 --> 00:19:08.740
The attacks.

00:19:08.740 --> 00:19:14.299
All those terrible flesh mountains were relentless,
bombarding the site night after night, trying

00:19:14.299 --> 00:19:17.100
to drag people out and expose them to the
light.

00:19:17.100 --> 00:19:21.750
It’s why Mobile Task Force operatives were
stationed along the perimeter with heavy weaponry,

00:19:21.750 --> 00:19:26.060
even though, short-staffed as they were, these
operatives were few and far between.

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:30.039
One of them, Commander Lewis, sat and stared
into the distance, keeping an eye out for

00:19:30.039 --> 00:19:32.919
more of the flesh mountains through the sights
of his rifle.

00:19:32.919 --> 00:19:35.420
That’s when he noticed a familiar shape.

00:19:35.420 --> 00:19:36.760
Almost like a giant peanut.

00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:39.830
Sure he must be seeing things, Lewis rubbed
his eyes.

00:19:39.830 --> 00:19:43.770
And in that moment, the thing he thought he’d
seen was behind him.

00:19:43.770 --> 00:19:47.960
It snapped his neck with a familiar, satisfying
crunch just as quickly.

00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:51.330
Just for a moment, it seemed that all was
right with the world again.

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:57.990
If SCP-173 could smile, it would smile and
think, “It’s good to be back.”

00:19:57.990 --> 00:20:04.210
Now go check out “SCP-173 Origin Story - How
173 Got to Site-19” and “When Day Breaks

00:20:04.210 --> 00:20:09.259
SCP-096” for more of the two utterly bizarre
anomalies from today’s video!

